  "title": "Libet shows late reflection, not that free will is an illusion",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "9ad8c607-0a58-42c2-9f5b-8680e0f30ff8",
      "text": "Libet's delay between premotor activation and the reported decision to move is usually read as showing free will is an illusion. It shows only that the reflexive re-representation of the self starting a movement comes later than the affective self actually starting it.",
